      "id": "sol.amc-8-2000-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "In \\(\\triangle AFG,\\) the two base angles are equal and \\(\\angle A=20^\\circ,\\) so\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} \\angle AFG &= \\angle AGF \\\\ &= \\frac{180^\\circ-20^\\circ}{2} \\\\ &= 80^\\circ. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nSince \\(\\angle AFG\\) and \\(\\angle BFD\\) form a straight angle, \\(\\angle BFD=100^\\circ.\\)\n\nIn \\(\\triangle BFD,\\) \\(\\angle B+\\angle D=180^\\circ-100^\\circ=80^\\circ.\\)\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the isosceles triangle \\(AFG\\) first",
        "Then use the angle sum of \\(\\triangle BFD\\)"
      ],
